From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:30:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] AROS: Intuition/GLA graphics window, pthreads OpenThreads

osgViewer gets a windowing system "AROS" (the default when the target
is AROS): GraphicsWindowAROS opens an Intuition window on the default
public screen and a GLA context in it, and turns IDCMP messages into
osgGA events (keys through a raw key table and MapRawKey, mouse
buttons, motion, NewMouse wheel codes, resize, close gadget). Cursor
hiding, pointer warp through input.device, window title, rectangle and
focus requests are implemented; shared contexts and pbuffers are not.

OpenThreads was not built at all for AROS (the pthreads backend sits
under IF(UNIX), which the AROS platform file does not set): it is now
built on AROS's pthread library.

The AROS platform file sets a variable named AROS, so the window system
test compares the variable's name and not its expansion.

Run on AROS pc-x86_64 in QEMU (softpipe, GL 3.3 and llvmpipe, GL 4.6):
window, rendering, keys with qualifiers, buttons, wheel, resize, close,
undecorated, hidden pointer and pointer warp.
